# A dev server's settings, read from `.env` (copy this file to it), which
# git ignores. A worktree with no `.env` of its own reads its main
# checkout's. Nothing here is needed: without a test key, login uses an
# in-memory stand-in that emails nothing (source/backend/infra/README.md),
# and the toolbar doesn't show, since nothing would keep its comments.

# A test key of this app's project on Superforge Infra (sf_test_…), from the
# project's keys on superforge.studio's dashboard. Its logins go through
# Infra's test mode, which emails nothing and answers the code instead, and
# the toolbar's comments reach the project's board, marked as a test's.
INFRA_TEST_KEY=
